+
+## Candidate
+
+- Staged independent local vault (`maj-vaj-vault`) and enrollment operator (`maj-vaj-credential-operator`); a root-owned systemd-provided Fernet KEK, private separate SQLite database, authenticated local peer, bounded no-export protocol, exact paired replacement/removal and verification before mutations. Only status, enrollment and local removal. No access to actual exchange credentials or venue adapter, no real connection verification, no trading-enabled or wallet slots. Local removal does not revoke a key at the provider. No automated KEK rotation or production encrypted backup/recovery. Legacy dev dashboard compatibility retained; installed qualification dashboard disables its vault.
+- Both opt-in services use fixed unit-specific credentials directory, locked mode/owner requirements, no secret environment bootstrap, core dumps disabled and Linux non-dumpable protection. Public data unit has explicit vault/qualification token mount restrictions; shared UID still not a substantive identity boundary. Local dashboard bearer remains accessible to unrelated processes with the desk UID; qualification-only marker renamed `paper-dashboard-qualification-enabled`. Do not use actual credentials or production tokens with it. No remote TLS/production authentication offered. New deployment units staged, not enabled automatically.
+- Offline synthetic test harnesses require explicit disposable-guest opt-in, QEMU/loopback, and pristine vault credentials for new runs. Setup assumes root-mounted read-only `/mnt/deps` with source/unit files; not production provisioning. These extra test-harness invocation safeguards were added after the executed runtime acceptance; no runtime source or service change afterward. Enrollment CLI prompts using non-echoing interactive terminal, separate operator principal; installed programmatic synthetic enrollment qualified, interactive human CLI not independently exercised.
