+- Genuine offline Debian systemd QEMU child of prior qualified guest: changed runtime files and units compared byte-for-byte on deployment, explicit-marker refusal, dedicated identities, independent credential file and DB denial, no plaintext read/export, reject secret phrase and partial pair, authenticated HTTP status and disabled credential write, concurrent pair rotation, persistent restart, local removal. Final matrix verified runtime vault file denial, same-UID dashboard memory denial, **confirmed same-UID dashboard bearer-file exposure**, and scanned DB/WAL, process args/environment, HTTP responses and installed journals for raw/hex/base64 synthetic markers. No marker observed in scanned surfaces; the bearer-file exposure is a distinct intentional adversarial access test and an open failure, not an overall pass.
+- Actual dashboard-initiated public market-only backup completed, no synthetic marker or desk/vault DB or credential key file in scanned backup. Worker process exited before environment observation; live child inspection remains open. Existing local worker and data handoff regressions passed; installed research handoff, browser persistence, notification channels and all egress paths not exhaustively scanned.
+- Actual installed fault matrix: wrong KEK refused without replacing DB; correct original KEK restores; corrupted ciphertext refused unchanged; controlled encrypted fixture restore succeeds; synthetic slot removed. All five checkpoints passed; this is not production/operator-approved encrypted backup restoration. Core limits verified. Named services stopped and runtime socket and private credential mount retired. Guest base SHA256 unchanged and qemu-img check no errors.
+- Initial installed startup rejected legitimate systemd 257 root:root ACL-protected 0440 credentials. Corrected exact unit-path/owner/mode compatibility. Fresh dashboard fixture needed an existing transfer-group membership for the entry fence, then a full-schema fresh disposable database rather than the prior minimal financial recovery fixture; the earlier fixture retained in the child overlay. Initial backup harness inspected wrong response field and timed out although backup completed; corrected rerun passed. Initial debug output enabled only temporarily for synthetic startup error and then removed. Final runtime source tested after corrections.
